"mini_hurdle_progression_phase_1_title" = "Phase 1: First 11-12 wickets";
"mini_hurdle_progression_phase_1_body" = "Start with 11-12 wickets to establish rhythm before running the full chain. Current plan: wicket 12 spacing is %@, about %@ of this plan's target longest spacing; wicket 12 is about %@ from start, and wicket 1-12 spans about %@.";
"mini_hurdle_progression_phase_2_title" = "Phase 2: Extend to 16 wickets";
"mini_hurdle_progression_phase_2_body" = "Once rhythm, landing, and posture are stable, extend to the first 16 wickets. Current plan: wicket 16 spacing is %@, about %@ of this plan's target longest spacing; wicket 16 is about %@ from start, and wicket 1-16 spans about %@.";
"mini_hurdle_progression_phase_3_title" = "Phase 3: Full 21 wickets";
"mini_hurdle_progression_phase_3_body" = "In the full 21-wicket setup, the final 3 wickets use the target longest spacing %@. Current plan: wicket 21 is about %@ from start, wicket 1-21 spans about %@; leave at least %@ run-out beyond the final wicket.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_title" = "On-field quality checks";
"mini_hurdle_quality_subtitle" = "Coach rhythm, landing, and speed quality first, then decide whether spacing should go up.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_detail_toggle" = "Show observation details";
"mini_hurdle_quality_1" = "The result should still look like good sprinting: hips stay tall, contacts stay active, and rhythm stays continuous.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_2" = "If the athlete reaches forward, lands clearly in front of the body, leans back, or loses speed, the spacing is too aggressive.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_3" = "If the athlete turns the drill into a deliberate high-knee hurdle action instead of sprinting through the marks, shorten the spacing or reduce the hurdle count.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_4" = "Only add more hurdles or move upward through Clark's range after the athlete consistently lands near the center of each mark.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_5" = "Time the reps once mechanics are stable so you can confirm that velocity is actually improving. If speed quality does not improve, do not keep lengthening the spacing.";
"mini_hurdle_quality_6" = "For the coach, this is stride-length management and force application. For the athlete, it should feel like running through fast and clean, not lifting into a hurdle action.";
